{"parentUuid":"8a1c9d69-a7f2-40be-af58-f8a16bd06745","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6ceed360-d6ad-4766-ba2d-4e6be6c75a36","agentId":"afcd6d73916c3b3e0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FUV6jA1KmQjtGEDBL8n96s","type":"tool_result","content":"Do squat movement speed and accommodating resistance differentially affect jump power and squat strength?\n\n## Population and context\n\n- Forty-eight male NCAA Division I baseball, track, football, and basketball athletes.\n- Sixteen athletes per group.\n- All had prior resistance and plyometric experience.\n\n## Study design and methods\n\n- Twelve-week randomized group intervention after three weeks of familiarization.\n- Groups used slow squats, fast squats, or fast squats plus elastic bands.\n- Other lower-body resistance, sprint, and plyometric programming was similar.\n\n## Key findings\n\nfrost-2010-a-biomechanical-evaluation-of-resistance.md:49:- Bands may sustain acceleration and late-phase force or velocity, but the review states that improved transfer to sport had not been demonstrated and much acute evidence showed no difference from load-matched free weights. [p. 21]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"49a32425-6f08-4743-8853-4f0fedb63c36","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:20:02.490Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Do squat movement speed and accommodating resistance differentially affect jump power and squat strength?\n\n## Population and context\n\n- Forty-eight male NCAA Division I baseball, track, football, and basketball athletes.\n- Sixteen athletes per group.\n- All had prior resistance and plyometric experience.\n\n## Study design and methods\n\n- Twelve-week randomized group intervention after three weeks of familiarization.\n- Groups used slow squats, fast squats, or fast squats plus elastic bands.\n- Other lower-body resistance, sprint, and plyometric programming was similar.\n\n## Key findings\n\nfrost-2010-a-biomechanical-evaluation-of-resistance.md:49:- Bands may sustain acceleration and late-phase force or velocity, but the review states that improved transfer to sport had not been demonstrated and much acute evidence showed no difference from load-matched free weights. [p. 21]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[],"moreFiles":0,"shared":true}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8a1c9d69-a7f2-40be-af58-f8a16bd06745","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
