heuristic--use-pulleys-and-dumbbells-for-spiral-diagonal-pnf-patterns.md"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffrDRq3iYG5RUpndRYYe","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ef89f066-a13b-4077-9e67-cfbd3e8cf288","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:23:28.520Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"ef89f066-a13b-4077-9e67-cfbd3e8cf288","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"189515d2-55e8-482a-8b52-f518760b72bc","agentId":"afcd6d73916c3b3e0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014LhsGDn6LBCrbeZtqsGu7D","type":"tool_result","content":"1","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4a0b7744-a5c0-4d16-9620-a1a96879dfd7","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:23:28.865Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--use-pulleys-and-dumbbells-for-spiral-diagonal-pnf-patterns.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":17,"oldLines":7,"newStart":17,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," **Why it works** — Siff's reason is pattern fidelity: PNF patterns \"stimulate more thorough involvement and motor development than the less-than-optimal patterns imposed by the abundance of linear or cam machines\" (PDF p. 418 / printed p. 407). Machine design \"imposes body positions, postures and activation of pivots which usually differ considerably from those recommended by PNF and compromise the effectiveness and safety of the exercise\" (PDF p. 421 / printed p. 410). He calls the belief that machines offer \"greater stability and safety for beginners than free weights\" \"A major error,\" and concludes \"instructors must always 'spot' for the users of machines as well as free weights\" (PDF p. 421 / printed p. 410)."," ","-**When to apply** — When choosing assistance exercises for rotational or overhead athletes, prefer cable and dumbbell versions that let the limb cross the midline and rotate. In 7.5 Siff lists other PNF methods to graft onto ordinary training: \"pre-stretch, exercising of agonists and antagonists, use of static and dynamic conditions, cheating to compel stronger muscles to help the weaker ones, optimal timing, use of full-range specific patterns of diagonal-spiral motions (details in Knott & Voss, 1977), application of maximal resistance throughout the non-ballistic movement range, and commencement of motion in the strongest range,\" which \"integrate very naturally into the extensive scheme of bodybuilding and weightlifting methods\" (PDF p. 430 / printed p. 419, checked against the page image). The traffic runs both ways: before his 1989 talk, \"nor did many physiotherapists know that some of the bodybuilding and weightlifting methods could be valuable in the rehabilitation setting\" (PDF p. 429 / printed p. 418, checked against the page image). Eric's baseline: \"Training time is deliberately weighted toward high motor-unit-recruitment core/ballistic movements (squats, cleans, jumps, throws, sprints); single-joint assistance work is kept to a small share of total volume.\" (`docs/method-baseline.md`, line 104, Inferred (transcript + slides)). Inference: this heuristic applies inside that small assistance share; it does not argue for replacing the barbell core lifts.","+**When to apply** — When choosing assistance exercises for rotational or overhead athletes, prefer cable and dumbbell versions that let the limb cross the midline and rotate. In 7.5 Siff lists other PNF methods to graft onto ordinary training: \"pre-stretch, exercising of agonists and antagonists, use of static and dynamic conditions, cheating to compel stronger muscles to help the weaker ones, optimal timing, use of full-range specific patterns of diagonal-spiral motions (details in Knott & Voss, 1977), application of maximal resistance throughout the non-ballistic movement range, and commencement of motion in the strongest range,\" which \"integrate very naturally into the extensive scheme of bodybuilding and weightlifting methods\" (PDF p. 430 / printed p. 419, checked against the page image). The traffic runs both ways: until the 1989 talk, the book says, \"nor did many physiotherapists know that some of the bodybuilding and weightlifting methods could be valuable in the rehabilitation setting\" (PDF p. 429 / printed p. 418, checked against the page image). Eric's baseline: \"Training time is deliberately weighted toward high motor-unit-recruitment core/ballistic movements (squats, cleans, jumps, throws, sprints); single-joint assistance work is kept to a small share of total volume.\" (`docs/method-baseline.md`, line 104, Inferred (transcript + slides)). Inference: this heuristic applies inside that small assistance share; it does not argue for replacing the barbell core lifts."," "," **When NOT to apply** — Siff says it \"does not imply that barbell and machine training should be avoided\": they \"can be used effectively under special circumstances, sometimes to cause intentional deviations from PNF patterns to adapt the body to potentially harmful actions which may occur in real sporting situations\" (PDF p. 421 / printed p. 410). No comparative data are given for the ranking or for the joint-loading claims about named machines. The \"excessive loading\" judgment on pec-decks and leg extensions is Siff's opinion in this passage. Inference: in rehab settings where Athletic Medicine wants a fixed path, a machine's constraint can be the point."," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--use-pulleys-and-dumbbells-for-spiral-diagonal-pnf-patterns.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ef89f066-a13b-4077-9e67-cfbd3e8cf288","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
