{"parentUuid":"2ba05617-258d-49e0-9488-6cee139f29a8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"189515d2-55e8-482a-8b52-f518760b72bc","agentId":"afcd6d73916c3b3e0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CPr68QYveB3mTzPe4qwaWv","type":"tool_result","content":"3","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"598305a2-8487-4747-b483-237101c0329e","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:28:13.944Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"3","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch7b_applied.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":49,"oldLines":7,"newStart":49,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," 1. **Fix 4(1) is half right.** Fig 7.10 is on PDF 423 / p.412, as the review says. But item (b)'s \"(PDF p. 424)\" was attached to the text quote \"near the beginning\", and that quote is on PDF 424 / p.413 (the \"If we examine Figure 7.10\" paragraph, seen on the image). So item (b) now carries both locators: the figure at 423 and the quote at 424. Item (a) now cites the table at PDF 423 and the \"some three times greater\" text at PDF 424."," 2. **Fix 3, CR repetitions.** The review gives \"a few\" for CR and \"several\" for SRHR. PDF 417 says CR \"is repeated several times\" and is \"continued gently for a few repetitions\". The entry quotes both for CR, and \"several repetitions\" for SRHR (PDF 418).","-3. **Fix 7: `contested` not set.** The two sections do address the same question (which muscles produce trunk flexion and rotation), so I recorded both with pages. But 7.4.1 is a list of movers and never says \"only\" or \"solely\"; 7.4.2 adds the obliques to flexion and multifidus to rotation rather than reversing anything. That is X against X-plus-more, not X against not-X, which is the brief's trigger for `contested`. The heel-raise entry in this batch records the same pattern (7.4.1 plantarflexion list without FHL, 7.4.2 adds it) under `supported`, and the review accepted that. The reasoning is labelled Inference in the entry.","+3. **Fix 7: `contested` not set.** The two sections do address the same question (which muscles produce trunk flexion and rotation), so I recorded both with pages. But 7.4.1 is a list of movers and never says \"only\" or \"solely\"; 7.4.2 adds the obliques to flexion and multifidus to rotation rather than reversing anything. That is X against X-plus-more, not X against not-X, which is the brief's trigger for `contested`. The heel-raise entry in this batch records the same pattern (7.4.1 plantarflexion list without FHL, 7.4.2 adds it) under `supported`, and the review accepted that. The reasoning is labelled Inference in the entry. Note: the review itself asked only that both pages be recorded, which was applied; the `contested` question came from the coordinator rule."," 4. **Missing idea 1, elbow note.** The review says forearm rotation happens at the radioulnar joints. The book's note itself says \"the radius and ulna twist about one another\" (PDF 429), so the book does describe the radioulnar twist; the error is only the phrase \"at the wrist\". The source note is worded that way."," 5. **Fix 5, Frost quote.** Frost's late-phase-force point is paraphrased from the vault brief, not put in quote marks, because the brief is a summary, not Frost's text."," 6. **Optional items not applied.** The optional rows for GO entries (hypertrophy items 7 and 9 pointer, core-stability link) and the optional rows for flagged entries (Fig 7.5 caption oddity in the PNF framework, the \"detrimental\" source note in the functional entry, \"text layer\" wording) were not applied, following the ch5b precedent. The PNF framework's \"Quotes from PDF pp. 414-418 are from the text layer\" sentence stays, as the review allows; the new quotes I added from PDF 415-418 say \"checked against the page image\"."]},{"oldStart":87,"oldLines":6,"newStart":87,"newLines":8,"lines":[" framework--four-forms-of-accelerated-powermetrics.md: [even more forceful than the load dropping and catching methods] 2"," claim--trunk-rotation-is-driven-by-the-obliques-not-the-erector-spinae.md: [Bilateral action of rectus abdominis and psoas] 1"," claim--trunk-rotation-is-driven-by-the-obliques-not-the-erector-spinae.md: [Source note on the 7.4.1 summary (Inference] 1","+case-study--fradd-free-weight-isokinetic-and-combined-elbow-flexion.md: [Table 7.1, PDF p. 423 / printed p. 412; text, PDF p. 424 / printed p. 413] 1","+claim--trunk-rotation-is-driven-by-the-obliques-not-the-erector-spinae.md: [rates the claim `supported`] 1"," ```"," "," Old phrases, count over all 14 scoped files (all 0; \"confidence: untested\" remains in 6 other 7b entries by design and is 0 in the Fradd file):"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch7b_applied.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2ba05617-258d-49e0-9488-6cee139f29a8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
